bic_trace_step.reason:
The function `loongson_gpio_init_irqchip` introduced in this commit allocates memory for `chip->irq.parents` using `devm_kcalloc` but incorrectly checks `chip->parent` for NULL instead of `chip->irq.parents` on the following lines:

	chip->irq.parents = devm_kcalloc(&pdev->dev, data->intr_num,
					 sizeof(*chip->irq.parents), GFP_KERNEL);
	if (!chip->parent)
		return -ENOMEM;

This allows a failed memory allocation of `chip->irq.parents` to go undetected, leading to a potential NULL pointer dereference when accessing `chip->irq.parents[i]` later in the function.
